  "id": "perceived-behavioral-control",
  "term": "perceived behavioral control",
  "definition": "Perceived behavioral control is a person’s sense of how much control they have over carrying out a behavior. In the theory of planned behavior, it is one of the main factors shaping intentions and, along with those intentions, helps explain actual behavior.",
