      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define perceived behavioral control as “a person’s sense of how much control they have over carrying out a behavior”; it only describes it as a construct related to “perceptions of behavioral control.”",
        "The rest of the definition (that, in the theory of planned behavior, it is used with attitudes and subjective norms to predict intentions, and intentions plus perceptions of behavioral control account for variance in actual behavior) is supported by the packet, but the first sentence contains an unsupported substantive characterization."
